m/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/1688","id":7296640,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcyOTY2NDA=","user":{"login":"eloraburns","id":35443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns","html_url":"https://github.com/eloraburns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-07-27T03:14:59Z","updated_at":"2012-07-27T03:14:59Z","body":"`how=\"mean\"` works:\n\n```\nIn [5]: df.resample(\"T\", how=\"mean\")\nOut[5]: \n                      0\n2012-01-01 00:00:00   1\n2012-01-01 00:01:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:02:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:03:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:04:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:05:00   2\n```\n\nI have no idea what numpy is up to, though:\n\n```\nIn [6]: import numpy as np\n\nIn [7]: df.resample(\"T\", how=lambda x: np.percentile(x, 50))\nOut[7]: \nEmpty DataFrame\nColumns: array([], dtype=int64)\nIndex: array([], dtype=object)\n```\n\nI can't seem to make it misbehave here, but with some Actual Data with data absent for several of the resampled intervals, I can get numpy to explode with the same stack trace as:\n\n``` python\nnp.percentile([], 50)\n# ...\n# ValueError: operands could not be broadcast together with shapes (0) (2) \n```\n\nI can certainly work around that in the lambda by short-circuiting on an empty list-like thing being passed in, but I don't think I should have to.\n\nFor this _particular_ case, I can just do this with expected results:\n\n```\nIn [8]: df.resample(\"T\", how=np.median)\nOut[8]: \n                      0\n2012-01-01 00:00:00   1\n2012-01-01 00:01:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:02:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:03:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:04:00 NaN\n2012-01-01 00:05:00   2\n```\n\nI can't fathom why `np.median(…)` is different from `np.percentile(…, 50)`. Maybe that's just a numpy thing? :)\n\nThanks!\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/7296640/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"eloraburns","id":35443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns","html_url":"https://github.com/eloraburns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eloraburns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":22530227,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjI1MzAyMjc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/events/22530227","actor":{"login":"wesm","id":329591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTU5MQ==","avatar_url"